================================================================================
                        EX00 — Mommy, when I grow up, I want to be a bureaucrat!
================================================================================

WHAT THIS EXERCISE COVERS:
  - Orthodox Canonical Form (OCF)
  - Nested exception classes (classes INSIDE a class)
  - Throwing and catching exceptions with try/catch
  - const attributes + initializer lists
  - Operator << overloading
  - Encapsulation (private attributes, public getters)

GRADE SYSTEM REMINDER:
  - Grade 1   = HIGHEST (best bureaucrat)
  - Grade 150 = LOWEST  (worst bureaucrat)
  - increment = grade goes UP   = number goes DOWN  (e.g. 5 -> 4)
  - decrement = grade goes DOWN = number goes UP    (e.g. 5 -> 6)

================================================================================
                         REMAINING BUGS IN YOUR CODE
================================================================================

[BUG 1] operator<< — Typo: "gureaucrat" instead of "bureaucrat"
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your current code in Bureaucrat.cpp:
      os << b.getName() << ", gureaucrat grade " << b.getGrade() << ".";

  Should be:
      os << b.getName() << ", bureaucrat grade " << b.getGrade() << ".";

  Just a typo — "gureaucrat" → "bureaucrat"

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

[BUG 2] Copy constructor — Unnecessary self-check + should use initializer list
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your current code:
      Bureaucrat::Bureaucrat(const Bureaucrat& other) : name(other.getName()){
          if (&other != this){
              this->grade = other.getGrade();
          }
      }

  The self-check (&other != this) is pointless in a copy constructor.
  A copy constructor ALWAYS creates a NEW object from another — `this`
  can never equal `other` because `this` didn't exist before.

  Cleaner version:
      Bureaucrat::Bureaucrat(const Bureaucrat& other) : name(other.name), grade(other.grade) {}

  Self-check is only useful in operator= (assignment), not copy constructor.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

