================================================================================
                              TRAPS / PITFALLS
================================================================================

  TRAP 1: Confusing increment/decrement direction
    "increment" means BETTER grade → smaller number
    "decrement" means WORSE grade  → bigger number

  TRAP 2: const name
    `name` is const → you CANNOT assign to it after construction.
    You MUST use the initializer list.

  TRAP 3: Self-check in copy constructor vs operator=
    - Copy constructor: self-check is USELESS (object is brand new)
    - operator=: self-check IS useful (a = a is possible)

  TRAP 4: The subject says name is CONST
    This means operator= can NEVER copy the name (on purpose).
    operator= should only copy grade. This is by design.

================================================================================
                              TRAPS / PITFALLS
================================================================================

  TRAP 1: Confusing increment/decrement direction
    "increment" means BETTER grade → smaller number
    "decrement" means WORSE grade  → bigger number
    Most bugs in this exercise come from mixing this up.

  TRAP 2: const name
    `name` is const → you CANNOT assign to it after construction.
    You MUST use the initializer list: Bureaucrat(...) : name(n) { }
    If you forget, the copy constructor silently gives an empty name.

  TRAP 3: Exception classes must inherit from std::exception
    And override what() — you already do this correctly.

  TRAP 4: Checking grade validity AFTER assigning
    Always validate BEFORE letting the object exist in a bad state.
    Your param constructor is correct (check after assign is fine in
    constructor since the object doesn't "exist" yet if you throw).

  TRAP 5: The subject says name is CONST
    Your hpp has `const std::string name` — good.
    But this means operator= can NEVER copy the name (on purpose).
    operator= should only copy grade. This is by design.
